class.description:
Use this node in place of [HTTPRequest] to instrument outgoing HTTP and HTTPS requests. It wraps an internal [HTTPRequest] and exposes its request methods, configuration properties, and completion signal. It inherits [Node], not [HTTPRequest].
Each request starts an [code]http.client[/code] span under the active [SentrySpan], if one exists. The SDK adds distributed tracing headers according to [member SentryOptions.trace_propagation_targets] and records HTTP breadcrumbs. Configure span sampling with [member SentryOptions.traces_sample_rate].
The span records the request method, host, request body size, response status, and response body size when available. Recorded URLs omit credentials, query strings, and fragments. Request and response body contents are not added to the span or breadcrumb.
Add the node to the scene tree before calling [method request] or [method request_raw]. Each instance handles one request at a time; use separate instances for concurrent requests. The span ends automatically when the request completes, is cancelled, or the node leaves the scene tree.
[b]Warning:[/b] Godot forwards tracing headers when following redirects, but propagation targets are checked only against the initial URL. See [member max_redirects] before requesting URLs that may redirect outside a trusted destination.
[codeblock]
func _ready() -> void:
	var scores_request := SentryHTTPRequest.new()
	add_child(scores_request)
	scores_request.request_completed.connect(_on_scores_received)
	var error: Error = scores_request.request("https://example.com/scores")
	if error != OK:
		push_error("Could not start the scores request: %s" % error_string(error))
func _on_scores_received(result: int, response_code: int, _headers: PackedStringArray, body: PackedByteArray) -> void:
	if result == SentryHTTPRequest.RESULT_SUCCESS and response_code == 200:
		print(body.get_string_from_utf8())
[/codeblock]
[b]Note:[/b] Call this node's methods from the main thread, even when [member use_threads] is enabled.
[b]On Web:[/b] Requests follow the browser's CORS rules. Cross-origin servers must allow any tracing headers sent by the SDK. See [url=https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/godot/tracing/distributed-tracing/dealing-with-cors-issues/]Dealing with CORS Issues[/url].
To learn more, visit [url=https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/godot/tracing/]Tracing documentation[/url].
